  "M grid uses the exact values 1e-4 * 2^(k/2), k = -1..5 (the spec's table prints them rounded to 3 digits).",
  "Seed of realisation r at (L, M) = 120000 + 1000*index(L) + 10*index(M) + r, r = 0..499, index(L) = 0 for L = 40 and 1 for L = 100, index(M) = 0..6 in ascending M, exactly as the spec's formula. Note: with r up to 499 the formula's seed ranges overlap ACROSS M values within one L (e.g. (index(M)=1, r=0) and (index(M)=0, r=10) share seed 120010), so neighbouring M points share initial grids and random streams (common random numbers); within one (L, M) point all 500 seeds are distinct, and L = 40 and L = 100 never share seeds. The spec's remark 'so streams never overlap' holds across L only. The formula is applied as written.",
  "G_max = N(2 + M N/2) is not an integer; each realisation runs floor(G_max) generations. Absorption is checked at the end of every generation (RPSSpatialModel.run), so 'absorbed by G_max' == absorbed at a generation <= floor(G_max).",
  "Each realisation: RPSSpatialModel(rows=L, cols=L, mobility=M, selection_rate=1, reproduction_rate=1, neighborhood='von_neumann', init_mode='random', seed, kernel='numba'); run(n_steps=floor(G_max), record_every=floor(G_max)+1). kernel='numba' is the compiled loop checked bit-identical to the reference loop (tests/test_rps_numba_kernel.py).",
  "Diagnostic D1 (G = N) is read from the primary runs: absorbed by generation N, i.e. absorption generation <= N (the primary runs use the same seeds and M and run at least 2N generations).",
  "Diagnostic D2 = our code at mobility M/2 run to floor(N(2 + (M/2)N/2)) generations, same seeds as the primary point at M. The diagnostics are evaluated with the same three conditions as the primary rule and are reported only.",
  "Optional L = 200 (spec: 'run only if the budget allows', 30-45 CPU-h) is not run.",
  "Wilson 95% interval with z = 1.959964."
